SUMMARY:The Art of Yoga | Summer-Fall Series 2026
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Museum for a harmonious blend of artistic inspiration and mindful movement! Our Saturday sessions are from 9:30–11am.  Experience how close looking at art and practicing yoga in the beautiful spaces of the Museum can foster relaxation and connection. \nEach yoga session includes a guided mindful looking session in one of the Museum’s current exhibitions. After class\, you’re invited to the John & Robyn Horn Education Center (level 3) for a complimentary cup of tea and artful conversation. \nAll levels are welcome. Please bring your own yoga mat. No mat\, no problem\, the Museum has some extra mats to lend. Loose-fitting clothing is recommended\, ensuring ease of movement as you flow through your practice. \n\nBenefits: \n\nMindful Connection: connect with the present moment as you flow through your practice in relation to a thought-provoking artwork.\nArtistic Inspiration: take advantage of practicing yoga in one of the most inspiring interior spaces in Asheville. Fuel your creativity and enhance the mind-body connection while meeting other artful yogis.\n\nPractical Tips: \n\nArrive a little early to settle into the Museum’s ambiance and find your preferred spot in the gallery.\nSpace is limited; advance registration is required.\n\nRegister Now \nPlease enter through the Staff Entrance to the left of the building. \n 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-yoga-fall-summer-series-2026/2026-10-10/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/DSC_1624-1-360x360-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
