SUMMARY:Rising Stars Concert with Quartet Nova Lux
DESCRIPTION:Rising Stars Concert is a collaboration between the Asheville Chamber Music Series and the Asheville Art Museum\, featuring North Carolina musicians embarking on a major concert career. The event is sponsored and made possible by Heidi DuBose. \nQuartet Nova Lux:  \n\nHyejin Kim\, violin\nAaron Lipsky\, clarinet\nKyle Johnson\, cello\nYeonju Lee\, piano\n\nQuartet Nova Lux was formed in 2025 by graduate students at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music.  Its members have appeared as soloist with the Indianapolis Symphony\, “The President’s Own” United States Marine Band\, and have performed with the Nashville Symphony\, New World Symphony\, Indianapolis Chamber Orchestra and Chattanooga Symphony.  They have also appeared as featured soloists and in chamber concerts in South Korea\, Japan\, France\, Czechia\, and the United States. \nProgram: \n\nOliver Messiaen’s Quartet for the End of Time\nPhillip Rhodes’ Following Picasso (A Fantasy After Stravinsky)\n\nPurchase Tickets
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/rising-stars-concert-with-quartet-nova-lux/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Performance
